"""
Author: Stefan Peidli
Title: Snakemake workflow for SYMPHONY experiment HEPA.
Last Updated: 11.09.2025
Run: snakemake
Create DAG: snakemake --forceall --dag | dot -Tpdf > ../results/pipeline/snake_dag.pdf
Create Rulegraph: snakemake --forceall --rulegraph | dot -Tpdf > ../results/pipeline/snake_rulegraph.pdf
Description:
    This snakemake workflow starts does the following:
    - Upstream processing
        - Download FASTQ files from BaseSpace
        - Run FastQC / MultiQC on the FASTQ files
        - Trim the FASTQ files with a custom script
        - Align the trimmed FASTQ files to the guides with HISAT2
        - Count the number of reads per guide using samtools
        - Merges the counts into a single table "SYM_HEPA_counts.csv"
    - Downstream processing
        - Runs MAGeCK
        - Runs BAGEL2
        - Runs Gscreend
    All user configuration is done in the configuration/config.yaml file.
"""

